        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="799" ezremote:identifier="intro" name="Summary" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/"><paragraph>Open source content management, maintained by the Exponential Foundation and 7x</paragraph></section>
        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/" ezremote:id="800" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/"><paragraph>Exponential is an open source content management platform and development framework. Version 6.0.15 runs on PHP 7.4 to 8.5 and on MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, SQLite, MongoDB and Oracle Database, and it powers everything from a personal site to multilingual, multi-site installations.</paragraph><paragraph>The Exponential Foundation and its community develop, document and support the platform. 7x maintains the code, publishes the releases and offers hosting, support and development services. Everything is GPL licensed: you can read the code, adapt it and extend it, and you are never tied to one vendor.</paragraph><section><header>Content first</header><paragraph>Content classes describe your content field by field, and the templates decide how it looks. The same article can appear on the web, in a feed, in an app through the REST API or as a static page on any web host.</paragraph></section><section><header>Made for editors</header><paragraph>The website toolbar (expwt) lets editors change a page where they read it. The administration interface adds drafts, versions, translations, an image picker and an assistant that suggests text and alt texts, always staged for review.</paragraph><section><header>Layouts and planning</header><paragraph>Exponential Layouts places blocks in the zones of a page, with rules that decide which layout a page gets, and lets editors plan what each block shows.</paragraph></section><section><header>Collaboration</header><paragraph>Workflows, approval and notifications keep a team in step, and every change is recorded in the audit log.</paragraph></section></section><section><header>Fast and secure</header><paragraph>Exponential Velocity keeps PHP workers warm and serves pages from its cache. Two-factor sign-in, "Verify it's you" for sensitive actions, content security policies and form tokens protect the site.</paragraph></section><section><header>Open technology</header><paragraph>Extensions add modules, datatypes, template operators and workflow events. Composer installs them, and the console (./console) runs installs, deploys, migrations and user management. Start with the <link href="https://doc.exponential.earth">documentation</link> and the extensions on <link href="https://projects.exponential.earth">projects.exponential.earth</link>.</paragraph></section><section><header>Support and community</header><paragraph>Ask questions and share solutions on <link href="https://share.exponential.earth">share.exponential.earth</link>, report problems on the <link href="https://issues.exponential.earth">issue tracker</link> and follow the code on <link href="https://github.com/se7enxweb/exponential">GitHub</link>.</paragraph></section></section>
